{
  "id": "02-rotting-oranges",
  "title": "Rotting Oranges",
  "track": "Graphs",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "topics": [
    "graphs"
  ],
  "source": "canonical Rotting Oranges concept; description, examples, and tests re-authored",
  "description": "The input is a grid where each cell holds 0 for empty, 1 for a fresh orange, or 2 for a rotten orange. Every minute, any fresh orange sharing an edge with a rotten one rots too. Return the number of minutes until no fresh orange remains, or -1 when some fresh orange can never rot. A grid without fresh oranges takes 0 minutes.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= number of rows <= 100",
    "1 <= number of columns <= 100",
    "grid values are only 0, 1, or 2"
  ],
  "parameters": [
    "grid"
  ],
  "functionName": "minutes_to_rot",
  "starterCode": "def minutes_to_rot(grid):\n    # grid[i][j]: 0 empty, 1 fresh, 2 rotten. Return minutes or -1.\n    ...\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": {
        "grid": [
          [
            2,
            0,
            1
          ],
          [
            1,
            1,
            1
          ],
          [
            0,
            1,
            1
          ]
        ]
      },
      "output": 4,
      "explanation": "The rot spreads wave by wave and reaches the far corner on minute 4."
    },
    {
      "input": {
        "grid": [
          [
            2,
            1,
            0
          ],
          [
            0,
            0,
            1
          ]
        ]
      },
      "output": -1,
      "explanation": "The orange in the bottom right has no rotten neighbor chain at all."
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "All rotten oranges start rotting their neighbors at the same time: this is one search with many starting points.",
    "Seed a queue with every rotten orange at minute 0; each wave of the queue marks one more minute of spread.",
    "Track the count of fresh oranges; when it hits zero, return the minutes elapsed. Fresh oranges left unreachable mean -1."
  ],
  "solution": "Multi-source breadth-first search: seed the queue with every rotten orange, and each wave rots the fresh neighbors of the current wave. The answer is the number of waves until the fresh count reaches zero, or -1 if fresh oranges remain. O(rows * cols) time and space.",
  "solutionCode": "def minutes_to_rot(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    queue = []\n    fresh = 0\n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if grid[i][j] == 2:\n                queue.append((i, j))\n            elif grid[i][j] == 1:\n                fresh += 1\n    if fresh == 0:\n        return 0\n    minutes = 0\n    while queue and fresh > 0:\n        minutes += 1\n        following = []\n        for x, y in queue:\n            for nx, ny in ((x + 1, y), (x - 1, y), (x, y + 1), (x, y - 1)):\n                if 0 <= nx < rows and 0 <= ny < cols and grid[nx][ny] == 1:\n                    grid[nx][ny] = 2\n                    fresh -= 1\n                    following.append((nx, ny))\n        queue = following\n    return minutes if fresh == 0 else -1\n",
  "bruteForceCode": "def minutes_to_rot(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    minutes = 0\n    while True:\n        freshly_rotten = []\n        any_fresh = False\n        for i in range(rows):\n            for j in range(cols):\n                if grid[i][j] != 1:\n                    continue\n                any_fresh = True\n                for nx, ny in ((i + 1, j), (i - 1, j), (i, j + 1), (i, j - 1)):\n                    if 0 <= nx < rows and 0 <= ny < cols and grid[nx][ny] == 2:\n                        freshly_rotten.append((i, j))\n                        break\n        if not any_fresh:\n            return minutes\n        if not freshly_rotten:\n            return -1\n        for x, y in freshly_rotten:\n            grid[x][y] = 2\n        minutes += 1\n",
  "failureHint": "hidden tests include no fresh oranges, no rotten oranges, and unreachable fresh oranges",
  "expectedComplexity": {
    "time": "O(m * n)",
    "space": "O(m * n)"
  },
